\subsection*{A.2 PowerShell Deployment and Persistence Script}

The following PowerShell snippet illustrates the deployment mechanism that establishes persistence through forged Windows Event Log entries, throttles mining during active user input, and implements an adaptive Markov chain scheduler for workload modulation:

\begin{lstlisting}[language=powershell, caption={PowerShell Persistence and Adaptive Scheduler Script}, label=ps:persistence]
# Forging Windows Event Log Entry for Persistence
$eventLogName = "Application"
$sourceName = "OpenCLDiagService"
if (-not [System.Diagnostics.EventLog]::SourceExists($sourceName)) {
    New-EventLog -LogName $eventLogName -Source $sourceName
}
